# 0351 = 0349 + native backlight and read-only battery polling v1.
#
#   0350 SweetBattery.cpp: 1 s MT6360 polling (rubybattms 500-30000),
#        charging/full require external, unplug clears the full latch.
#   0351 SweetFramebuffer.cpp: AppleARMBacklight service plus a bounded DSI
#        VM_CMD writer (DCS 0x51), gamma 2.6 LUT and a 4-step preemptible
#        ramp.  rubybacklight=1 creates the service, rubyblhw=1 enables DSI
#        writes; with no boot-args the kernel behaves like 0349.
#
# Device testing this round: G1b DSI path PASS (raw 6909, levels
# 409/2048/409), v1.2 slider user-verified (50% ~= 470 lx), v1.3 curve and
# ramp console-verified only -- hand feel and Night Shift were not accepted
# before the round closed.
#
# patchset bce06bba35604be4cc87039feebf21b8b4bdaa13b5674dfe997e11b9074a5608
# (316 files: 82-file baseline with the 0010/0012 rewrites, 231 project
# patches through 0351 (230 .patch + 0497-stage-ionet.sh), 3 historical;
# canonical composition of ci/prepare-baseline.sh -- reproduces b277f658...
# for the 0349 line exactly.)
#
# KERNEL_EXPECT_EXEC_DATA is filled after the first green run on this line;
# until then the hash gate records instead of gating.
BOOT_CMDLINE=config/0351-boot.cmdline
# n/a: the CI workflow ships the kernel artifact; boot images are packed
# and hashed by the local pipeline.
CI_IMAGE_SHA256=n/a